    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d116-a5">

                <pb facs="0209" n="101" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg101"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 5 in No.
                    130.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Notice of the captain of the port.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-12-20"><hi rendition="#italic">December 20,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">To his excellency the Italian
                        consul:</hi></p>
                <p>I have the honor to ask your excellency to take the necessary measures that the
                    ships of your nationality that are anchored between the Ilha das Cobras and the
                    Ilha das Enxadas and those in any point near these islands may withdraw with the
                    greatest speed from such anchorages, to leave free range to the legal batteries
                    and forts so that they may attack the revolted ships which go and seek shelter
                    alongside the foreign ships and fire thence upon the land forces.</p>
                <p>I repeat to his excellency, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">José Pinto do Suz</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Captain of the port.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
